BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fa-39775@ev3nts.filmakademie.de
DTSTAMP:20261006T230635Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20261001T103000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20261001T111500
SUMMARY:Alumni Case Study: Condenaditos: There Is No Manual
LOCATION:Filmgalerie Empfang
DESCRIPTION:Pflicht\nDozent*innen: Matisse Gonzalez\, Stefan Michel\n\nCond
 enaditos: There Is No Manual\n\nCondenaditos is a feature film in developm
 ent between Studio Seufz (Germany)\, Ikki Films (France)\, and Amora Films
  (Spain) and\, as it turns out\, an unlikely case study.\n\nIt tells the s
 tory of Kiki\, the youngest daughter of a Bolivian family living under a g
 enerational curse. When she discovers the curse traces back to her grandfa
 ther's involvement in the Bolivian dictatorship\, she sets out against her
  family's wishes to find forgiveness and break the curse. A 2D-Animated So
 ft Coming-of-Age Dark Fantasy Political Horror Feature Film for adults.\n\
 nIn this talk\, we'll walk through the project's trajectory: where it came
  from\, the obstacles we've faced\, and how we're navigating them. But the
  honest starting point is this: there is no manual for a project like ours
 . No clear precedent\, no established path\, no one to tell us the right s
 teps to take.\n\nAnd yet\, here we are: funded by MFG\, CNC\, The Minitrai
 té\, and now Creative Europe Media.\n\nhttps://ev3nts.filmakademie.de/use
 r/student/?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-01
CATEGORIES:Pflicht
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
